---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Using Communication Data for End-of-Season Hindsighting - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a href="/case-studies" class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <svg class="mr-1 h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Outdoor Apparel</span>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Using Communication Data for End-of-Season Hindsighting</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Sustainability-focused outdoor apparel brand with a 12-18 month product cycle</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Senior sourcing leadership responsible for multi-season strategy</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">No data-driven way to answer "why were we late?" at the end of a season — root cause analysis required manual reconstruction from scattered communications</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">At the end of every season, sourcing leadership at this outdoor apparel brand wanted to answer a simple question: "Why did we miss something?" The answer was never simple. Delays could originate anywhere in a 12-18 month product cycle — a late fabric approval, a slow lab dip turnaround, a production capacity conflict the factory didn't surface until the last minute. Tracing the root cause required manually reconstructing the communication timeline from email, WhatsApp, and Slack.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">A senior sourcing leader at the brand — with experience at multiple major retailers including a $4.6 billion childrenswear company — described the post-season review as more art than science. Teams relied on memory and anecdote. The person closest to the issue might have left or moved roles. The email thread where the warning signs first appeared was buried in an inbox alongside hundreds of other messages. Meaningful process improvement was difficult without reliable data about what actually went wrong and when.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">This made it hard to distinguish between systemic issues (a vendor that consistently delays at the same production stage) and one-off problems (an unusual material shortage). Without that distinction, every season's mistakes felt new.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Marker links every supplier communication to the relevant milestone in the product calendar. When a season ends, leadership can run a hindsight analysis that traces each delay back to the specific communication where the issue first appeared — the email where a supplier flagged a capacity concern, the WhatsApp message where a delivery date was revised, the Slack thread where the team discussed an alternative but didn't act on it.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Over multiple seasons, patterns emerge: which suppliers consistently flag issues late, which milestones are most vulnerable to slippage, and which internal handoffs tend to create bottlenecks. This transforms the post-season review from a memory-based exercise into a data-driven process improvement cycle. The sourcing team can make structural changes — adjusting timelines, reallocating vendors, or adding buffer to high-risk stages — based on evidence rather than intuition.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Every delay traceable back to the specific communication where the issue first appeared, across all channels</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Systemic vendor issues distinguished from one-off problems through multi-season pattern analysis</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Internal handoff bottlenecks identified — where the delay started with the supplier vs. where it stalled internally</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Post-season reviews transformed from memory-based exercises into evidence-based process improvement</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">See how Marker turns communication data into actionable season-over-season insights.</p>
        <a href="/book-demo" class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2">Book a Demo</a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
